title=Object+Source+Lighting+for+Miniatures%3A+Simple+OSL+Guide&slug=object-source-lighting&content=%3Ch1%3EObject+Source+Lighting+for+Miniatures%3A+Simple+OSL+Guide%3C%2Fh1%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EShort+answer%3A%3C%2Fstrong%3E+OSL+means+painting+light+as+if+it+comes+from+an+object+on+the+model%3A+pick+the+light+source%2C+then+tint+every+surface+facing+it+with+the+light+colour+%E2%80%94+strongest+at+the+nearest+point%2C+fading+with+distance.+Two+glazes+and+one+highlight+colour+are+enough+for+a+convincing+effect.+Reflection%2C+not+brightness%2C+is+the+secret.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cblockquote+class%3D%22wp-block-quote%22%3E%3Cp%3E%3Cem%3EDisclosure%3A+Some+links+on+this+page+are+affiliate+links+%E2%80%94+if+you+buy+through+them%2C+we+may+earn+a+small+commission+at+no+extra+cost+to+you.%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Fblockquote%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EWhat+Is+OSL+%E2%80%94+and+Why+It+Elevates+Your+Models%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EObject+Source+Lighting+is+the+painted+illusion+that+a+model+%3Cem%3Eemits%3C%2Fem%3E+light%3A+a+torch%2C+a+plasma+coil%2C+a+warp+portal.+Done+well%2C+OSL+makes+viewers+see+light+instead+of+paint.+It%27s+the+single+highest-impact+technique+in+the+hobby+%E2%80%94+and+it%27s+less+about+skill+than+about+discipline%3A+consistent+light+direction%2C+controlled+intensity%2C+restrained+coverage.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+1%3A+Determine+Light+Direction+and+Falloff%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EFix+three+things+before+painting%3A%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Col%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EWhere%3C%2Fstrong%3E+the+light+source+sits+on+the+model%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EWhich+surfaces+face+it%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+mentally+trace+a+straight+line+from+the+source+to+every+panel%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EHow+far%3C%2Fstrong%3E+the+light+reaches+%E2%80%94+falloff+is+fast%3B+light+rarely+travels+more+than+10%E2%80%9315+mm+convincingly%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Fol%3E%0A%3Cp%3EMark+the+facing+surfaces+with+a+light+pencil+dot+if+you+need+to.+OSL+fails+when+light+lands+on+surfaces+that+couldn%27t+possibly+see+the+source.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+2%3A+Layering+Transparent+Glazes%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cul%3E%0A%3Cli%3EMix+your+glow+colour+as+a+%3Cstrong%3Ethin+transparent+glaze%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%28glaze+medium+or+heavily+thinned+paint%29%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3EApply+1+glaze+to+the+outermost+zone+of+the+lit+area%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3EApply+2%E2%80%933+glazes+on+the+mid+zone%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3EApply+4%E2%80%936+glazes+%E2%80%94+or+a+stronger+mix+%E2%80%94+on+surfaces+immediately+adjacent+to+the+source%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Ful%3E%0A%3Cp%3EBecause+glazes+are+transparent%2C+the+underlying+paint+still+reads+through%3A+this+is+what+makes+OSL+look+like+light+on+a+surface+rather+than+paint+on+top+of+it.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+3%3A+The+Source+Itself%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3EPaint+the+emitting+object+at+maximum+brightness%3A+base+colour+%E2%86%92+bright+tone+%E2%86%92+near-white+core.+The+source+must+always+be+the+brightest+point+of+the+model%2C+or+the+whole+illusion+collapses.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EStep+4%3A+Avoiding+Common+Over-Glowing+Mistakes%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cul%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EThe+%22spray+tan%22+error%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+tinting+every+surface+equally.+Light+has+direction%3B+distance+matters%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EToo+saturated+colour%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+real+light+washes+surfaces+out%3B+your+glazes+should+lighten%2C+not+just+colour%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3ELight+on+impossible+surfaces%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+underside+of+an+arm+facing+away+from+the+torch+breaks+the+illusion+instantly%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EGlow+stronger+than+the+source%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+reflected+light+is+always+dimmer+than+the+emitter%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Ful%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EWhen+to+Use+Which+Effect%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cfigure+class%3D%22wp-block-table%22%3E%3Ctable%3E%3Cthead%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Cth%3EEffect%3C%2Fth%3E%3Cth%3EBest+tool%3C%2Fth%3E%3Cth%3EDifficulty%3C%2Fth%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3C%2Fthead%3E%3Ctbody%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3ESmall+glow+%28eyes%2C+coils%29%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EDirect+painting+%28see+%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fworkbench%2Fglowing-plasma-effects%2F%22%3Eglow+guide%3C%2Fa%3E%29%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EBeginner%3C%2Ftd%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3EMedium+OSL+%28torch%2C+weapon%29%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EGlazes+on+facing+surfaces%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EIntermediate%3C%2Ftd%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3Ctr%3E%3Ctd%3ELarge+OSL+%28portal%2C+engine%29%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EAirbrush+or+extensive+glaze+work%3C%2Ftd%3E%3Ctd%3EAdvanced%3C%2Ftd%3E%3C%2Ftr%3E%3C%2Ftbody%3E%3C%2Ftable%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%0A%3Ch2%3ERecommended+Brushes+and+Glaze+Mediums%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cul%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EGlaze+medium%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+single+most+useful+OSL+purchase%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3ESoft+Taklon+glaze+brush+%28%232%29%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+holds+a+thin%2C+even+coat%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EKolinsky+detail+brush+%28%230%29%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+for+reflected+streaks%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%3Cstrong%3EMatte+varnish%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+kills+any+accidental+shine+before+you+start+glazing%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Ful%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cem%3E%28Affiliate+links+%E2%80%94+support+the+workbench+by+buying+through+them.%29%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EFAQ%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EIs+OSL+too+advanced+for+beginners%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3ESimple+two-glaze+OSL+on+one+small+light+source+is+a+beginner-accessible+technique.+Save+the+20-glaze+portal+engines+for+model+number+fifty.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EWhat+colour+should+I+use+for+OSL%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3EMatch+the+light+source%27s+logic%3A+fire+%3D+warm+orange%2C+plasma+%3D+blue%2Fcyan%2C+warp+energy+%3D+violet+or+storm-green.+The+reflected+colour+must+always+match+the+source+hue.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EDo+I+need+an+airbrush+for+OSL%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3ENo+%E2%80%94+an+airbrush+speeds+up+large+surfaces%2C+but+glazes+handle+everything+a+tabletop+model+needs.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EHow+do+I+combine+OSL+with+weathering%3F%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Cp%3EWeather+first%2C+glow+second.+OSL+light+passes+over+grime+naturally+%E2%80%94+but+paint+order+matters%3A+pigments+and+chipping+under+glazes%2C+never+on+top.%3C%2Fp%3E%0A%3Ch2%3EContinue+on+the+Workbench%3C%2Fh2%3E%0A%3Cul%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fworkbench%2Fglowing-plasma-effects%2F%22%3EHow+to+Paint+Glowing+Plasma+Effects%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+beginner+version+of+this+technique%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fworkbench%2Feasy-weathering-techniques%2F%22%3EEasy+Weathering+Techniques%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+how+grime+and+glow+interact%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fworkbench%2Fairbrush-for-beginners%2F%22%3EAirbrush+for+Miniatures%3A+Beginner+Setup%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+when+you%27re+ready+to+speed+up%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3Cli%3E%F0%9F%91%89+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Flore%2Fwarp-travel-explained%2F%22%3EWarp+Travel+Explained%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%E2%80%94+the+lore+behind+violet+portal+light%3C%2Fli%3E%0A%3C%2Ful%3E%0A%3Cblockquote+class%3D%22wp-block-quote%22%3E%3Cp%3E%3Cstrong%3EOSL+is+the+difference+between+a+painted+model+and+a+scene.%3C%2Fstrong%3E+One+light+source%2C+two+glazes%2C+full+commitment.+%3Cstrong%3E%3Ca+href%3D%22%2Fshop%2Fpaints%2F%22%3EShop+glaze+mediums+%E2%86%92%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E+%3Cem%3E%28affiliate+links%29%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Fblockquote%3E&status=publish